This directory contains a model of a #327 incandescent lamp for use
with LTSpice.  It also contains a bulb stabilized Wien bridge oscillator
that uses it.  The oscillator is based on the NE3332 op amp.

See YouTube videos:

   https://youtu.be/8FEQJIkZJYo
and
   https://youtu.be/HP5jtEx2Chc
  
LTSpice Model

BULB_327_WB.sub is an LTSpice model of a #327 lamp, a 28V / 40mA
incandescent bulb.
   
To use it, go to your LTSpice projects directory (Documents/LTSpice on
Windows), create directory lib/sub within it and place the .sub file
there.  Then, open the .sub file in LTSPice and right click on the
line that begins with "SUBCKT".  You should see a menu that allows you
to create a symbol automatically for the lamp. Do so.

Then, restart LTSpice and you should be able to place the lamp like
any other component.  You should find it in lib/sub in the place
component dialog.

Lamp Stabiized Wien Bridge Oscillator

Place file NE5532.lib into lib and put ne5532_wien_osc_bulb_wb_simpler.asc
into your LSpice project file (the one containing lib).  You can then
open the latter and start an LTSpice simulation.
